id: pm-f7shxf
title: Invalidate shared history projections when writers lack SQLite
description: A SQLite-less append followed by a Node indexed append can certify a projection with a current stream-size receipt while omitting the middle authoritative fact. The history stream retains all three entries. Every supported runtime must participate in the invalidation protocol so a later indexed writer cannot hide earlier facts.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-17T22:34:40.375Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T00:49:30.481Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-18T00:49:29.537Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T00:49:29.537Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce two projected facts versus three authoritative facts before the fix; Preserve all three facts after a later indexed append; Exercise real Bun and Node against one isolated tracker; Keep cursor and return shapes compatible; Retain portable committed invalidation and full-source quality gates
goal: project management = context management
objective: Preserve complete shared-workspace mutation facts across SQLite and non-SQLite producers
value: Bun and Node can safely share the same project context without silent event omissions
why_now: The second review concurrency controls independently reproduced a missing middle event in a three-append mixed-backend sequence.
parent: pm-lvyd
risk: medium
confidence: 95
resolution: "Route SQLite-less producers through invalidation, verify an incremental writer has a current authoritative base before advancing its receipt, and move the optional projection to generation6 so legacy size-certified omissions rebuild. Mark incompatible or stale caches untrusted without requiring unlink before authority progresses, including native legacy-reader contention."
expected_result: "Preserve every authoritative fact across indexed/SQLite-less writers and completed history merges, recover legacy incomplete caches, and retain portable nonblocking contention behavior."
actual_result: "Original and upgrade controls reproduce missing middle facts and legacy false certification before correction. All467 focused source tests pass with complete event-index coverage in diagnostics; linked omitted and legacy cohorts pass2/4 tests. Six current/legacy native contention cases preserve authority and safe recovery, including failures reproduced before retention. Real Node26.9/Bun1.4.3 public SDK consumers return three unique full facts matching authority and pass strict validation. Final-head full hosted coverage/static/analyzer admission remains mandatory; current local qualified CLI startup failures are recorded separately."
